{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q15426249","formula":"C₅₃H₆₀ClN₃O₁₆","hill":"C53H60ClN3O16","elements":["H","C","N","O","Cl"],"composition":{"C":53.0,"H":60.0,"N":3.0,"O":16.0,"Cl":1.0},"names":{"en":"Kedarcidin","uk":"Кедарцидін"},"descriptions":{"en":"Kedarcidin is a chromoprotein antitumor antibiotic first isolated from an Actinomycete in 1992, comprising an ansa-bridged enediyne chromophore (shown) as well as an apoprotein that serves to stabilize the toxin in the Actinomycete. Like other members of the enediyne class of drugs—so named for the nine-or-ten-membered core structure bearing an alkene directly attached to two alkynyl appendages—kedarcidin was likely evolved to kill bacteria that compete with the producing organism. Because it achieves this by causing DNA damage, however, kedarcidin is capable of harming tumor cells, as well.","uk":"Кедарцидін — хромопротеїн протипухлинний препарат вперше виділений з актиноміцетів у 1992 році. Кедарцидін, ймовірно, виробляється мікроорганізмами для вбивства конкурентних бактерій. Оскільки це досягається шляхом пошкодження ДНК кедарцидін здатний також завдавати шкоди пухлинним клітинам."},"fame":6,"pubchemCid":6477354,"mass":1030.5,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC1C(C(CC(O1)OC\\2COC(=O)C(CC3=NC(=C(C=C3)OC4C=C5C#C/C2=C\\C#CC6C5(C4OC7CC(C(C(O7)C)O)(C)O)O6)Cl)NC(=O)C8=C(C=C9C=C(C(=C(C9=C8)OC)OC)OC(C)C)O)O)N(C)C","inchikey":"GFTRTMUGNRZABD-IPBVOBEMSA-N","iupac":"N-[(15E)-6-chloro-24-(4,5-dihydroxy-4,6-dimethyloxan-2-yl)oxy-14-[5-(dimethylamino)-4-hydroxy-6-methyloxan-2-yl]oxy-11-oxo-4,12,20-trioxa-7-azapentacyclo[13.6.2.25,8.13,21.019,21]hexacosa-1,5,7,15,25-pentaen-17,22-diyn-10-yl]-3-hydroxy-7,8-dimethoxy-6-propan-2-yloxynaphthalene-2-carboxamide","classes":[{"qid":"Q59199015","names":{"en":"group of stereoisomers","ru":"группа стереоизомеров","uk":"група стереоізомерів"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"6477354","atoms":133,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure"